{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions","id":1032631,"title":"Goetic Familiar Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-16T07:05:40-08:00","id":1032631,"title":"Goetic Familiar Questions","content":"I have a mechanical question about Goetia in general, and then about using the Familiar spell in a specific instance.<br /> <br /> First, the Mage book talks about Goetia not having natural manifestations while also talking about how they appear in Mind-attuned twilight if they come to the material world. Is this just an oversight that they aren't called out as having Twilight Manifestation like Ghosts and Spirits, or do I have to do magic to pull one out of the Astral Realms?<br /> <br /> Second, could I travel into my own Oneiros and seek out a Goetia to cast the Familiar spell on, then have the Familiar hold spells in my mind using the new &quot;Connected&quot; connection?<br /> <br /> The first one threw me off, the second one is a yes in my reading but figured I'd ask if I missed anything while I clarified the Twilight Manifestation issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:27:50-08:00","id":1032645,"title":"","content":"1- I have to assume it is a mistake just by a, the reading on what twilight is (state ephemeral exist in, in the material unless manifest) and b, if they don't have twilight form they must be by default manifest which I do not see any hint that such was the intent.<br /> <br /> 2- there is no reason for you to not be able to bind a familiar that way however you will be removing that Goetia from your mind and will lack that aspet untIL its returned iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:56:31-08:00","id":1032661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1032645#post1032645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- I have to assume it is a mistake just by a, the reading on what twilight is (state ephemeral exist in, in the material unless manifest) and b, if they don't have twilight form they must be by default manifest which I do not see any hint that such was the intent.<br /> <br /> 2- there is no reason for you to not be able to bind a familiar that way however you will be removing that Goetia from your mind and will lack that aspet untIL its returned iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! I thought it must just be a mistake to say ghosts and spirits naturally get it and Goetia get nothing, because the only reading I had for that would be that they can't leave the Astral realms without a Mage's help and that didn't really fit with what else was written.<br /> <br /> I was going to leave the Goetic Familiar inside my Oneiros and use it (and eventually them) as a stable of Spell Control slots. Since they have to be willing, I thought that would be a cool way to face and embrace the good and bad of my mage while gaining strength. They would basically control their own Familiar spells, then hold another one for me, since the Connected connection allows holding 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:00:40-08:00","id":1032664,"title":"","content":"The only part is can a non sleepwalker, can a Goetia take on spell control?<br /> Then what use will it be in your mind, why bind it at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:05:54-08:00","id":1032668,"title":"","content":"The first line of discussing spell control from other people is &quot;The truth is, technically, anyone with a sympathetic tie to a mage can carry spells for her.&quot; I assume that means any sympathetic tie with something that can meet the requirement of consenting to holding the spell and understanding that they are helping you. My ST has already ruled that the this works for a Ghost Familiar in the game. I am pretty new to ephemeral entities, but I think they're cool, so I wanted my new mage in this chronicle with 20 starting xp to be astrally focused. I suppose I could simply bargain with them if they are already sympathetically connected with at least a Strong connection to me, I just assumed I'd need to create the link with the Familiar spell because that's how we did it before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:45:01-08:00","id":1032689,"title":"","content":"The only place I can find reference to sharing spell control is in the section on sleepwalkers. However if in your game it has been ruled that it is the sympathy that is important or I'm just missing the right page, a familiar would have the required sympathy to hold two spells instead of one, even if it isn't from your own mind. After all a mage and their familiar have the highest rating of sympathy connection, equal to a mage's own soul stone.<br /> Other than not removing the Goetia aspect from your mind however I don't see the benifit of leaving your familiar in the astral. To hand off spell control it'd be easier to not need to enter the astral first, would it not? To also be able to utilize the fact that both you and your familiar can spend each other's essance/mana as your own fuel (even with the one loss per transfer) I feel it may require being within the same realm. Then the ability to cast through its senses without requiring the sympathetic range also seems lost to you, even if you can use it across a realm there is not much use to casting into the astral while you arent there - at least in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:29:30-08:00","id":1032713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M:tAw page 101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Familiar (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Effect: Your character has been bonded to a Familiar, an ephemeral entity (<b>a ghost, spirit, or Goetia</b>) that has agreed to partner her in exchange for safety from bleeding Essence. Design your familiar with the rules for ephemeral entities in Chapter Six; it may be wholly in Twilight or Fettered to an item or animal. Two dots in this Merit indicate a Rank 1 entity. Four dots indicate a Rank 2 entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>A familiar can be a Ghost, Spirit or Goetia, so I see no reason that a Spirit of Goetia couldn't work the same as a Ghost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M:tAw page 260</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entity has been bonded to a mage. It may use any other Manifestations freely, but is protected from Essence bleed. The entity and its bonded mage have a <b>Connected Sympathetic</b> link to one another, may use one another\u2019s senses with a reflexive action (casting magic through a Familiar requires a Reach for remote viewing, but does not require the Sympathetic Range Attainment), and can pass Mana and Essence between them \u2014 Mana given to the Familiar converts into Essence, and Essence given to the mage converts into Mana, but one point of the transferred resource is lost with the exchange. If an entity under the effects of Familiar is discorporated, it will reform in a location bearing the mage\u2019s Signature Nimbus.<br /> Causing the Condition: This Condition is created with the Familiar spell (p.183).</div> </div> </div> </div>All familiars have a Connected Sympathetic connection to the Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:14:04-08:00","id":1032870,"title":"","content":"The benefit of leaving your goetia familiar in the Astral is that you then have a means of influence in the astral without going there yourself. You can also cast your spells in the astral via your Connected Sympathy with your familiar, etc. There are a lot of benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:26:58-08:00","id":1033030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions#post1032631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, the Mage book talks about Goetia not having natural manifestations while also talking about how they appear in Mind-attuned twilight if they come to the material world. Is this just an oversight that they aren't called out as having Twilight Manifestation like Ghosts and Spirits, or do I have to do magic to pull one out of the Astral Realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be that Goetia can't naturally support themselves in the Material the way ghosts and spirits does (though they do require Essence to stay). Without a spell (such as Summon Goetia or Familiar) the Goetia might not be able to visit the material world without instantly being pulled back to where they came from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:36:40-08:00","id":1033039,"title":"","content":"Mages who project their minds out of their bodies don't assume a Twilight form, they're living mental images. They're invisible except to those who have attuned their sight to Mind attuned Twilight though. I assume that goetia who are in the Fallen exist in a similar state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:41:31-08:00","id":1033041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033039#post1033039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages who project their minds out of their bodies don't assume a Twilight form, they're living mental images. They're invisible except to those who have attuned their sight to Mind attuned Twilight though. I assume that goetia who are in the Fallen exist in a similar state.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, aren't you saying there that they exist in twilight? That is all twilight form covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:45:47-08:00","id":1033047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033041#post1033041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh, aren't you saying there that they exist in twilight? That is all twilight form covers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fine line distinction, but it does allow ephemeral entities to exist in Twilight without the Twilight Manifestation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:50:33-08:00","id":1033055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033047#post1033047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a fine line distinction, but it does allow ephemeral entities to exist in Twilight without the Twilight Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see where you are going with that. The only rebuttal is twilight form sets a ephemeral being's default state to twilight rather than material. Without that should a Goetia not be automatically manifested while in the material? After all, a mage projecting themselves is more comparable to a ephemeral being exerting their will to manifest since it is not their default state. However, it is a method of rectifying the exclusion of goetia from all manifestations including twilight form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:30:51-08:00","id":1033077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033055#post1033055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see where you are going with that. The only rebuttal is twilight form sets a ephemeral being's default state to twilight rather than material. Without that should a Goetia not be automatically manifested while in the material?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It can't be automatically manifested because goetia don't have manifestations.<br /> <br /> An image that appears only in a certain frequency of Twilight is not the same as having a Manifestation regardless of how irrelevant the difference appears to be. It also doesn't mean that somehow because it lacks a Manifestation that ties to Twilight it must somehow be visible in the Fallen.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-16-2017, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:48:20-08:00","id":1033088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033077#post1033077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It can't be automatically manifested because goetia don't have manifestations.<br /> <br /> An image that appears only in a certain frequency of Twilight is not the same as having a Manifestation regardless of how irrelevant the difference appears to be.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The last thing I will say (because I don't want to pull this further off topic):<br /> <br /> A) &quot;Without Manifestations or magic, ephemeral entities in the material world exist in the state of Twilight.&quot; MtAw pg 253.<br /> B) &quot;If the entity enters the material world, it does so in Twilight&quot; the description of twilight form.<br /> <br /> Either the Goetia Follows (A) and (B) despite by RAW not having twilight form manifestation. Because if (B) does not apply (A) is contradicted and a goetia would not enter twilight once it enters the material. In that sense if they do not have twilight form their default state is material, for they do not enter twilight upon entry without this manifestation. So I propose the far simpler alternative that goetia are meant to possess this lone manifestation so that it follows the general rules of ephemeral beings while still retaining the lack of natural manifestations otherwise. I feel it is the far cleanest solution to this discrepidency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T23:51:19-08:00","id":1033189,"title":"","content":"Re: Spell Control<br /> <br /> 'Anyone' implies it has to be a person.<br /> I don't think Goetia are people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:21:14-08:00","id":1033222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033088#post1033088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last thing I will say (because I don't want to pull this further off topic):<br /> <br /> A) &amp;quot;Without Manifestations or magic, ephemeral entities in the material world exist in the state of Twilight.&amp;quot; MtAw pg 253.<br /> B) &amp;quot;If the entity enters the material world, it does so in Twilight&amp;quot; the description of twilight form.<br /> <br /> Either the Goetia Follows (A) and (B) despite by RAW not having twilight form manifestation. Because if (B) does not apply (A) is contradicted and a goetia would not enter twilight once it enters the material. In that sense if they do not have twilight form their default state is material, for they do not enter twilight upon entry without this manifestation. So I propose the far simpler alternative that goetia are meant to possess this lone manifestation so that it follows the general rules of ephemeral beings while still retaining the lack of natural manifestations otherwise. I feel it is the far cleanest solution to this discrepidency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just follow the rules for Psychic Projection which neatly keeps inside the rules as presented and doesn't require your mental gymnastics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:38:26-08:00","id":1033228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033222#post1033222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or just follow the rules for Psychic Projection which neatly keeps inside the rules as presented and doesn't require your mental gymnastics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;mental gymnastics&quot; you're describing are &quot;the technical reading of how goetia interact with the Manifestation system is superseded by the fact that they're ephemeral beings who exist in Twilight in the material world.&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;or just&quot; process you're referring to is &quot;you use your highest Mental or Social Attributes to derive a PFR Attribute spread despite 'not having an ephemeral body' and needing to use magic (which doesn't use Attributes) to affect anything while you're in Twilight in this fashion.&quot;<br /> <br /> The vast majority of goetia do not inhabit the material realm and thus are generally a non-issue to anyone astrally projecting into the Twilight of the Mind Arcanum, but the Twilight Form Manifestation represents the default state of any ephemeral being in the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:46:47-08:00","id":1033231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033228#post1033228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;mental gymnastics&quot; you're describing are &quot;the technical reading of how goetia interact with the Manifestation system is superseded by the fact that they're ephemeral beings who exist in Twilight in the material world.&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;or just&quot; process you're referring to is &quot;you use your highest Mental or Social Attributes to derive a PFR Attribute spread despite 'not having an ephemeral body' and needing to use magic (which doesn't use Attributes) to affect anything while you're in Twilight in this fashion.&quot;<br /> <br /> The vast majority of goetia do not inhabit the material realm and thus are generally a non-issue to anyone astrally projecting into the Twilight of the Mind Arcanum, but the Twilight Form Manifestation represents the default state of any ephemeral being in the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't another interpretation of these rules be that Goetia <i>can't</i> access the material world at all, even in a Twilight state, unless given the Twilight Form manifestation via other magic, first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:56:08-08:00","id":1033233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1032631-goetic-familiar-questions?p=1033231#post1033231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't another interpretation of these rules be that Goetia <i>can't</i> access the material world at all, even in a Twilight state, unless given the Twilight Form manifestation via other magic, first?</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>already</i> can't access the material world at all without magic or other mysterious phenomena to facilitate their emergence. Requiring extra spells to allow an ephemeral being summoned to the material world to <i>be</i> an ephemeral being in the material world is a special kind of nonsensical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T01:57:50-08:00","id":1033235,"title":"","content":"Well they are able to be familiars somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T03:23:24-08:00","id":1033251,"title":"","content":"As I've already suggested: The spells that facilitates their passage could automatically grant them a proper Manifestation. It just that it ends when Goetic Summons or Familiar (the two most common spells) ends, in contrast to ghosts who will remain but suffer Essence bleed.<br /> <br /> The problem with using the rules of Psychic Projection is that it makes no sense that the entire ephemeral being (corpus and all) would be distilled into an image form that is otherwise only used for projected consciousnesses whose actual bodies are present elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}